+# Bug Fix: Product deletion breaks carts and order history
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T21:40:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Cart hydration now removes only lines whose catalog product was deleted and keeps even an empty cart available for recalculation, editing and checkout. Missing product additions and v2 SKU lookups now return 404, while order responses continue to use stored `OrderProduct` snapshot data and no order rows are touched.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java` | modified | Remove obsolete/deleted lines individually and keep the cart non-obsolete, including when no lines remain. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/cart/ReadableShoppingCartMapper.java` | modified | Defensively skip orphaned/obsolete lines during cart conversion. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Report an unknown SKU as `ResourceNotFoundException`. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v2/product/ProductApiV2.java` | modified | Translate a missing SKU result to `ResourceNotFoundException` (HTTP 404). |
+
+## Diff Highlights
+
+Deleted catalog lines are removed while iterating the hydrated cart, and the cart's obsolete flag is explicitly reset. The order mapper was already snapshot-first and null-safe for optional live-product enrichment, so no order persistence or mapping change was required.
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- No dedicated regression fixture was added; existing core and shop integration suites were run against the changed paths.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -DskipTests compile` → passed.
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am test` → passed; sm-core 28 run/0 failed/0 errors/13 skipped, sm-shop 33 run/0 failed/0 errors/8 skipped.
+- Manual checks: reviewed the delete, cart hydration, cart mapper, add-to-cart, order mapper and v2 SKU paths; no API server fixture was available for the exact delete/order lifecycle.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The assessment proposed adding focused deletion lifecycle tests. The repository's available suites contain no fixture for that complete sequence, so source changes were kept minimal and existing core/shop tests were used for compilation and regression coverage.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add a dedicated integration fixture covering product deletion followed by mixed/empty cart retrieval, checkout, order reads and 404 assertions.
